-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",300,{
[9569]="700173A7\n1\tBring Angmarim iron to Ornras at Echad Mirobel\030Collect Angmarim iron\tThe Angmarim can be found throughout Mirobel in southern Eregion, near the Elf-haven of Echad Mirobel. You should seek out Angmarim in Mirobel and collect proof that they travel with Angmarim Iron. If the fears of Ornras are true, the tide could easily turn against the Elves with the forging of great weapons on the enemy's side.\n",
[9570]="700173AC\n1\tDeliver the White Hand symbol to Gelirwen at Echad Mirobel\030Collect a symbol of the White Hand (quantity: see journal)\tA symbol of the White Hand may be found among the enemies throughout the lands around Echad Mirobel. Gelirwen wants to preserve the memory of the School at Tham Mírdain and save it from the befouling evil currently residing there. She will not risk lives without first knowing the enemies that are to be faced. She has asked you to obtain a symbol of the White Hand from among the enemies to help her learn about these foes.\n",
[9571]="7005AABC\n1\tDefeat hobgoblin sentries (total: 5)\tHobgoblin sentries patrol the roads near Stazg Vozag.\n2\tTalk to Klúso near Stazg Vozag\tKlúso is scouting near Stazg Vozag.\n",
[9572]="70025871\n1\tYou received a letter from the Crafting Guilds of Middle-earth inviting you to visit one of their apprentice trainers. You should seek out [see journal].\t\n",
[9573]="7006D1AD\n1\tSecure the Eastern Entrance of Iridír\tAs you clear areas of Iridír from attackers, raise the control point banner to signal the Dumûri.\n2\tSecure the Western Banner in Iridír\tAs you clear areas of Iridír from attackers, raise the control point banner to signal the Dumûri.\n3\tSecure the Northern Banner in Iridír\tAs you clear areas of Iridír from attackers, raise the control point banner to signal the Dumûri.\n",
[9574]="70026E75\n1\tTalk to Alun at the look-out camp\tAlun is encamped to the south-west, near a large bent tree. Bethan has asked you to talk to Alun if you wish to learn more about the people of Dunbog.\n",
[9575]="70015E18\n1\tLook for signs of the Company\030Find the Redhorn Gate\tThe Redhorn Gate lies to the north-east of Ruidhriel's camp. Ruidhriel has asked you to go up into the Redhorn Gate and look for signs of the Company where the snow and trees begin.\n2\tTalk to Ruidhriel\tRuidhriel is south and west of the Redhorn Gate, near the Burnt Tor. You should return to Ruidhriel and tell her what you found.\n",
[9576]="7005D39F\n1\tFind and defeat the Warg\tThe Warg prowls the highest tier in western Clovengap. Borghild has asked you to deal with a vicious Warg who blocks the army's progress.\n2\tSpeak to Nakrovak\tNakrovak is in eastern Clovengap. Nakrovak, a crystal-encrusted Warg, has asked you to listen to her tale.\n3\tDefeat the cub-snatchers (total: 4)\tNakrovak's cubs are held prisoner in eastern Clovengap. Angmarim sorcerers have cubnapped Nakrovak's litter! You should defeat the Angmarim!\n4\tRescue the Warg cubs\tNakrovak's cubs are held prisoner in eastern Clovengap. With the Angmarim defeated, you should release the Warg cubs.\n5\tReturn to Nakrovak\tNakrovak is in eastern Clovengap. You have freed Nakrovak's cubs. You should ensure they all made it back to her safely.\n",
[9577]="7004CE45\n1\tTalk to Frekur\030Talk to Orgrand\030Talk to Rikolf\030Talk to Olgat\030Talk to Ránnvig\tRikolf, Frekur, Orgrand, Ránnvig, and Olgat can be found in Lake-town. You should visit Rikolf, Frekur, Orgrand, Ránnvig, and Olgat to collect their payments.\n2\tTalk to Dagrun\tDagrun can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town. You should talk to Dagrun.\n",
[9578]="70046C29\n1\tClear overgrown branches from the roadways of North Ithilien (total: 12)\tOvergrown branches can be found along the southern roadways of North Ithilien. You should clear the roadways of overgrown branches as you make your way north to aid in the advance of the Host of the West.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have cleared a great deal of overgrown branches and plants from the roadways of North Ithilien.\n",
[9579]="7004799D\n1\tDefeat Orc overseers in Skoironk (total: 2)\tOrc overseers can be found within the sprawling caverns of Skoironk. You should defeat Orc overseers.\n2\tReturn to Candúr\tYou should return to Candúr, who can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.\n",
[9580]="70029B08\n1\tDefeat Orc-overseers (total: 4)\tOrc-overseers can be found throughout Isengard. Dagoras asked you to defeat the Orc-overseers keeping the labourers of Isengard in line.\n2\tTalk to Dagoras within the Ring of Isengard\tDagoras is within the Ring of Isengard. You should return to Dagoras with news of your success.\n",
[9581]="70059780\n1\tDestroy barricades at Overwine Hall\tBarricades can be found at Overwine Hall in the Wildwood. You should destroy barricades at Overwine Hall.\n2\tDestroy barricades at Overwine Hall (total: 6)\tBarricades can be found at Overwine Hall in the Wildwood. You should destroy barricades at Overwine Hall.\n",
[9582]="7005976B\n1\tDefeat foes at Overwine Hall\tFoes can be found at Overwine Hall in the Wildwood. You should defeat foes at Overwine Hall.\n2\tDefeat foes at Overwine Hall (total: 6)\tFoes can be found at Overwine Hall in the Wildwood. You should defeat foes at Overwine Hall.\n",
[9583]="7006C05E\n1\tDefeat zealots (total: 8)\tZealots of Zidemel can be found in TBD. TBD, a man living in Ghalburu, is worried about the violent zealots causing trouble in the TBD and has asked you to handle a few of their number.\n2\tReturn to TBD Anti-Zealot\tTBD Anti-Zealot can be found in Ghalburu. Return to TBD Anti-Zealot\n",
[9584]="70046899\n1\tGather supplies (total: 10)\tYou should gather the supplies scattered around Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\n2\tFill crates (total: 2)\tThe supply cart can be found at Aragorn's Pavilion. You should put the supplies in the crates next to the supply cart.\n3\tTalk to Angbor\tAngbor can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor. You should talk to Angbor.\n",
[9585]="7004E90A\n1\tPan for precious minerals in the Greylin River (quantity: see journal)\030Pan for precious minerals in the Forest River (quantity: see journal)\030Pan for precious minerals in the Heath River (quantity: see journal)\tThe Greylin, Forest, and Heath Rivers can all be found in Ered Mithrin. You should pan for precious minerals at all three rivers.\n2\tReturn to Skarháld\tYou should return to Hórin in Skarháld with the minerals you have panned.\n3\tSift through contents of your panning bag in a rinsing cask\tYou should sift through the contents of your panning bag in a rinsing cask, found in Skarháld.\n4\tBring the mithril flake to Hórin\tYou should bring the mithril flake to Hórin in Skarháld.\n",
[9586]="70041D74\n1\tStop as many pillagers from stealing treasures as you can\tStop the pillagers from escaping with Pelargir's ancient treasures. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[9587]="700428CA\n1\tStop as many pillagers from stealing treasures as you can\tStop the pillagers from escaping with Pelargir's ancient treasures. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[9588]="70034D02\n1\tCollect a log of wood\tThe wood for the Mead-hall fire pits are kept along the wall to Reeve Gárwig's left. Gárwig has requested a log be put on the fire. It seems to be harder and harder to keep the mead hall warm these days.\n2\tPut the log on the fire\tGárwig asked for the log be put on the fire-pit to his left. Gárwig has requested a log be put on the fire. It seems to be harder and harder to keep the Mead-hall warm these days.\n3\tTalk to Gárwig\tGárwig awaits his fate on the throne in the Mead-hall.\n4\tSend the messenger to Dunfast\tThe messenger which Gárwig asked you to send to Dunfast is waiting near the stables in Forlaw.\n5\tTalk to Cyneberg in Lornsettle\tCyneberg is keeping Gárwig company in Lornsettle, the Mead-hall of Forlaw.\n",
[9589]="7006BF07\n1\tSpeak with Sarnor near Vartúlin's upper path\tSpeak with Sarnor near Vartúlin's upper path and gather his water buckets.\n2\tGather Sarnor's buckets (total: 2)\tGather Sarnor's buckets. They are beside him on his left.\n3\tCollect water from Vartúlin's upper stream near the bridge\tCollect water from the upper stream and water the Veróthi near the bend in the path.\n4\tCollect more water from Vartúlin's upper stream near the bridge\tCollect water from the upper stream and water the Veróthi at the edge of Vartúlin.\n5\tSpeak with Avadhril\tSpeak with Avadhril in Vartúlin.\n",
[9590]="70030027\n1\tExplore Parphád.\tExplore Parphád\n2\tDefeat invaders within Parphád (total: 20)\tYou should defeat enemies within Parphád and spare the ruins further damage.\n3\tTalk to Ascbert\tYou should speak with Ascbert and inform him of your efforts in preventing further damage to Parphád's relics.\n",
[9591]="70030028\n1\tExplore Parphád.\tExplore Parphád\n2\tTalk to Ascbert\030Collect weathered parchment (total: 8)\tPieces of weathered parchment may be found in Parphád. You should collect pieces of weathered parchment and bring them to Ascbert.\n",
[9592]="70030022\n1\tDefeat the leader of the invaders in Parphád\tGangfinda stands nearby. You should ride Gangfinda to Parphád.\n2\tTalk to Ascbert\tHaving defeated the leader of the invaders in Parphád, you prepare to return to Ascbert and inform him of your success.\n",
[9593]="70026E46\n1\tTalk to the look-out to join the Dunlendings of Trum Dreng\tYou should speak with the look-out in the northern pass of Trum Dreng.\n2\tFind the village of Lhan Tarren\tLhan Tarren, the village of Elain of the Stag-clan, lies to the south of where you found her. You have been urged to seek the hospitality of the humble Caru-lûth clansmen while you pass through Trum Dreng.\n3\tFind Elain inside the village\tElain made it safely back to her village, Lhan Tarren. You should speak with Elain briefly before presenting yourself to the Elder of the Stag-clan in Trum Dreng.\n4\tTalk to the Elder of the Stag-clan\tThe Elder of Lhan Tarren is inside the bounds of the village. You should speak with the Elder, for he wishes to thank you for your kindness to Elain.\n",
[9594]="70017580\n1\tReturn to Armbeald in the Redhorn Lodes\030Collect the yellowed tooth\030Collect the chipped tooth\030Collect the stained tooth\030Collect the flat tooth\tThe Orcs suspected of taking the teeth are in the White Hand Orc-fortress in the Redhorn Lodes. Look for high-ranking Orcs in your search for the missing teeth. They should be defeated and their remains searched, and if any teeth are found, Armbeald in the Redhorn Lodes will wish to see them.\n",
[9595]="7000C378\n1\tFind the hidden entrance to Goblin-town\tBilbo Baggins described the location and advised you to use his description to find the hidden entrance to Goblin-town that he and the dwarves of Thorin's Company once came across on their journeys long ago. Bilbo Baggins would like you to help him correct the directions to Goblin-town that he has written in his book.\n2\tTalk to Bilbo Baggins at Rivendell\tBilbo Baggins is at the Last Homely House in Rivendell, south-west of Goblin-town. Having completed the task Bilbo set you to, you should return to him at Rivendell.\n",
[9596]="70061442\n1\tTravel to Waymeet\tWaymeet can be found to the north-east of Michel Delving in the Shire. Intent on recalling mail bound for Yondershire and conducting a test on the route to Nobottle, Postmaster Proudfoot has asked you to travel to Waymeet and talk to Postman Twofoot.\n2\tTalk to Postman Twofoot at Waymeet\tPostman Twofoot can be found at Waymeet in the Shire. You have arrived at Waymeet. You should talk to Postman Twofoot and inform him of Postmaster Proudfoot's request.\n3\tCollect the satchels of mail bound for Yondershire at Waymeet (total: 2)\tSatchels of mail bound for Yondershire can be found at Waymeet. Postman Twofoot has informed you that his assistant, Norbert Hogg, was preparing the satchels of mail for Yondershire at Waymeet but has likely misplaced them due to his fascination with pipe-weed. You should find and collect the satchels of mail bound for Yondershire at Waymeet.\n4\tDeliver the satchels to Norbert Hogg at Waymeet and relay Postman Twofoot's orders\tNorbert Hogg can be found somewhere around Waymeet in the Shire. Postman Twofoot has asked you to deliver the satchels of mail to his assistant, Norbert Hogg, and inform him to bring them to the Quick Post in Michel Delving. Norbert Hogg can be found somewhere at Waymeet, likely near a source of pipe-weed.\n5\tTalk to Postman Twofoot at Waymeet\tPostman Twofoot can be found at Waymeet in the Shire. After sending Norbert Hogg off to Michel Delving with the satchels for Yondershire, you should conduct a test of the Quick Post's route to Nobottle according to Postmaster Proudfoot's instructions. You should talk to Postman Twofoot at Waymeet.\n6\tPut Postmaster Proudfoot's hastily-scrawled letter into the empty satchel\tThe empty satchel can be found on Postman Twofoot's table outside the Quick Post in Waymeet. According to the Postmaster's instructions, Postman Twofoot has prepared an empty satchel for you. You should put Postmaster Proudfoot's letter into the empty satchel at Waymeet.\n7\tTalk to Postman Twofoot at Waymeet\tPostman Twofoot can be found at Waymeet in the Shire. You have prepared a satchel containing Postmaster Proudfoot's letter to be taken on the Quick Post's route to Nobottle. You should talk to Postman Twofoot.\n",
[9597]="70062131\n1\tTalk to Watcyn\tYou should tell Watcyn the truth about Rendal's past.\n2\tTalk to Rendal\tWatcyn has pleaded for you and Rendal to help him. You should talk to Rendal and decide on what to do.\n3\tFind Rendal near Gaervarad\tRendal plans to attack the captains in Gaervarad. You should meet with him there. Gaervarad is located to the south-west of Sírlond.\n4\tTalk to Rendal\tYou have found Rendal near Gaervarad. You should talk to him to discuss what to do next.\n",
[9598]="7002EEF9\n1\tBring the toy sword to Sperling at Eaworth\t\n2\tBring the toy sword to Sperling at Eaworth\tSperling is at Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale. You should bring the toy sword to Sperling and explain what happened.\n3\tTalk to Brunstan in Eaworth\tBrunstan is in Eaworth. You should let Brunstan know that you found Sperling's sword.\n4\tTalk to Getfleda in Eaworth\tGetfleda is in Eaworth. You should return to Getfleda and let her know that all is now well between Brunstan and Sperling.\n",
[9599]="7002BFAB\n1\tCollect Rushgore clay (total: 6)\030Collect Rushgore reeds (total: 6)\tThe burrow Gisalic mentioned lies to the north-east of the Woodman camp in the Rushgore. Gisalic asked you to collect reeds and clay from the burrow he saw nearby.\n2\tBring the reeds and clay to Gisalic at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore\tGisalic is at the Woodman camp at the heart of the Rushgore. You should return the materials you gathered to Gisalic and tell him of the insect infestation.\n",
[9600]="70008824\n1\tSpeak with Sergeant-at-Arms Ambeng at Lugazag\030Collect untreated leather-hides (total: 10)\tWild beasts with strong hides roam the Ettenmoors. The leather made from their hides will be useful to the war effort. Sergeant-at-Arms Ambeng asked you to seek out untreated leather from the wild beasts throughout the Ettenmoors.\n",
})
